```
The checker treats HOLD as a change from BUY, and it rejected ADD at conviction 4 the same way. Only BUY would match, and a stock we already own can't get a BUY. So any review of a holding within 30 days of buying it fails this check. Nothing genuinely new has happened since 2026-11-16:
- the Q3 results (10-28), the shelf filing (11-10) and the chair change (11-12) all came before that BUY;
- the price is down about 1%, well under the 10% that counts as a price move.

**Ways forward (your call):**
1. Change `check_docs.py` so it accepts HOLD or ADD at the same conviction as a match for an earlier BUY when the stock is now held. This is the proper fix.
2. Skip re-reviewing holdings within 30 days of buying them.
3. Let me add a `new_evidence` entry, which would misstate the evidence. I don't recommend it.

